# SIM-DIGEST v1 include=frame clockDelta ents <eN=name,pos,yaw,hp,st,ak,qi> pathJobs turns turnOrder draws
# entity-fields=name pos[3] yaw hp=cur/max st=entityState,moving,acted q=QUEUED ACTION COUNT (shipped Entity+0x314, the action deque's ELEMENT COUNT - ++ at 0x54ea71, -- at 0x54b637/0x54b672, never a 0/1 store; our side derives it from actions[] so it can be at most 4, and a shipped q above 4 beside our q=4 is deviation D-2, i.e. a DROPPED ORDER, not a digest bug - T-039 verdict, harness item 22; it is printed as a COUNT and was never a busy flag, which is why it left the st= triple) qi=EFFECT-INBOX COUNT (shipped Entity+0x2F0, the effect deque's live count - the field virt_meth_0x54ab00's busy predicate reads as != 0, T-074 §4e; our side derives it from inbox.fx[] - inbox-era state since P-CMBT steps 1-2 route damage through the inbox; the shipped side renders NA:absent-in-capture when its capture predates the inbox era, and a lockstep capture carrying numbered qi must name an r5 read) ak=ACTION CLASS NAMES: our side maps port kind->class in code, the original side maps [action+0x00] vftptr->class via artifacts/F3.json, UNKNOWN_VT=<ea> when unresolved and those are counted, never named | cap 12 entities, excess -> entsMore=1
# COMPARED=frame clockDelta ents eN.name/pos/yaw/hp/st/q/ak/qi pathJobs turns turnOrder draws | CONTEXT(after ' ctx:')=tickMs clock (ABSOLUTE) - printed, captured, NOT hashed: uptime and the shipped first-Update leap make both incomparable across processes, so the digest carries clockDelta (seconds elapsed since frame 0) as the comparable axis instead; promote a CONTEXT field in the comparator, never by re-running the session | caller-supplied=clock tickMs - a headless harness owns simulated time; the app path passes Host::TickMilliseconds (timeGetTime, machine uptime) and the world clock Gregorian::TotalSeconds, which STARTS AT 0 and grows by Update(ms)-last (mbr_0x48 initialises to 0 against an ABSOLUTE tick, so the first pump adds the whole uptime - see docs/f3/SimDigest.md); cross-context comparisons must pin both
# EXCLUDED=reaction-anim-id gfx-texture-slots gui-fragments voice-roll effect-rolls (presentation-side)
# WHY-draws-IS-IN: the reaction id stays out, but one global sequential LCG feeds both - 8 of the 18 shipped draw sites sit in sub_45C140 (docs/f3/CombatRngSeam.md) - so damage-draw COUNT shifts the reaction outcome. Counting draws is what keeps that coupling named instead of implicit; excluding the reaction id alone would be an unnamed coupling, not a separation.
# NA-means=the seam is not ported, NEVER =unchanged
# SEED-LIMIT: a parity run pins ONE captured LCG state, so it proves SAME-STATE parity, NOT same-seed-from-clock parity: identical under a pinned state and divergent in real time is a possible and meaningful outcome
# PROVES=self-consistency of our sim. DOES NOT PROVE=parity with F3.exe (needs T-028 + a bootable exe).
# SOURCES combat=ok paths=NA
